/-! # Projective normalization of a radical curve extension

Source: Stacks Project, etale-cohomology.tex, Tag 03PL (unit-root algebra);
pione.tex, Tag 0BQL (normal generic components); morphisms.tex, Tags 035B and 0AVK
(finite normalization) (blueprint: lem-sfb-radical-normalization-projective-etale).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Normalizing a smooth projective integral curve in the field generated by chosen radical
roots gives a normal integral projective curve, finite and surjective over the original
curve, and etale over the common unit locus.

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 03PL, 0BQL, 035B, 0AVK
(blueprint: lem-sfb-radical-normalization-projective-etale).

The two range conditions express regularity of each radicand and its inverse at every
point of U. They impose no nonemptiness condition on U. The field L is the specified
intermediate field of the given algebraic closure, not an arbitrary isomorphic extension.
The final equation identifies the canonical generic morphism with Spec of the function
field. Composing with fromNormalizationIn gives exactly the original map induced by F → L,
since toNormalization followed by fromNormalization is the defining generic morphism.
No geometric integrality or roots of unity in the base field are required.

Proof plan, following the eight steps of the node:
1. Finite type over K gives Noetherianity (lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian).
   Smoothness gives regularity (lem-weil-pbc-smooth-scheme-over-field-regular), hence
   normality (rem-pc-regular-normal). The affine fraction-field description and stalk
   localizations, with lem-weil-pbc-normal-domain-of-local-normal, make every nonempty
   affine coordinate ring A an integrally closed domain with fraction field F.
2. The normalization charts are Spec of the integral closures of A in L
   (def-fin-normalization-extension). By lem-weil-pbc-integral-closure-finite-extension-normal
   these are normal domains with fraction field L; their localizations are normal by
   lem-weil-pbc-localization-normal-domain. The canonical Spec L is dense in each chart,
   giving integrality. lem-sbc-normalization-generic-field identifies that very morphism
   with the generic morphism of Y, compatibly with its map to C.
3. lem-fin-normalization-extension-finite makes the normalization finite; lying over
   (pqf-lem-lying-over) on each affine chart makes it surjective.
4. Integral injective extensions preserve dimension
   (lem-weil-pbc-integral-injective-dimension-equal). Apply
   lem-pc-dimension-affine-open-cover to C and to its inverse-image cover to obtain dim Y = 1.
5. lem-fin-finite-over-projective over the affine Noetherian base Spec K gives a finite
   projective-space embedding of Y (def-kun-projective). Properness
   (lem-pc-projective-proper) supplies separatedness and finite type, so def-pc-curve applies.
6. On each nonempty affine open V in U, form the successive monic unit-root algebras.
   lem-sfb-unit-binomial-finite-etale gives finite etaleness at every stage; compose using
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-composition and lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation.
7. Evaluation at the chosen roots maps the generic algebra onto L: its image is a finite
   dimensional domain, hence a field (lem-weil-pbc-finite-dimensional-domain-is-field).
   The finite product decomposition of lem-sfb-finite-etale-normal-generic-components
   selects exactly one field factor, identified with L. Its normalization over V is finite
   etale, and is exactly the specified inverse image of V in Y.
8. Etaleness is local on the source (lem-weil-pbc-etale-local-on-source), so these affine
   assertions glue over U. The empty covering handles U empty; r = 0 gives the identity
   root algebra, and n = 1 makes each root algebra its base. -/
theorem radical_normalization_projective_etale
    (K : Type u) [Field K] (C : Scheme.{u})
    (q : C ⟶ Spec (.of K)) [IsSmoothProjectiveCurve q]
    (U : C.Opens) (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (hnK : IsUnit (n : K))
    (r : ℕ) (a : Fin r → C.functionFieldˣ)
    (hreg : ∀ (j : Fin r) (x : C), x ∈ U →
      (a j : C.functionField) ∈ Set.range (algebraMap (C.presheaf.stalk x) C.functionField) ∧
      (a j : C.functionField)⁻¹ ∈ Set.range (algebraMap (C.presheaf.stalk x) C.functionField))
    (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [Algebra C.functionField Ω] [IsAlgClosure C.functionField Ω]
    (α : Fin r → Ω) (hα : ∀ j : Fin r, α j ^ n = algebraMap C.functionField Ω (a j))
    (L : IntermediateField C.functionField Ω)
    (hL : L = IntermediateField.adjoin C.functionField (Set.range α))
    [FiniteDimensional C.functionField L] :
    (∀ y : C.normalizationIn L,
      IsDomain ((C.normalizationIn L).presheaf.stalk y) ∧
        IsIntegrallyClosed ((C.normalizationIn L).presheaf.stalk y)) ∧
    IsIntegralCurve (C.fromNormalizationIn L ≫ q) ∧
    IsHProjective (C.fromNormalizationIn L ≫ q) ∧
    IsFinite (C.fromNormalizationIn L) ∧ Surjective (C.fromNormalizationIn L) ∧
    Etale (C.fromNormalizationIn L ∣_ U) ∧
    ∃ e : Spec (.of L) ≅ Spec (C.normalizationIn L).functionField,
      e.hom ≫ (C.normalizationIn L).fromSpecFunctionField =
        (C.fromSpecOfAlgebraFunctionField L).toNormalization := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
